# Gives every @ExclusiveMeterRegistry test class an application context of its own, so a class that
# prunes the MeterRegistry in setup cannot reach the dozens of classes Spring would otherwise hand
# the same registry bean. This is the extension point Spring itself uses to isolate classes that
# declare bean overrides; see ExclusiveMeterRegistry and ER-0101.
org.springframework.test.context.ContextCustomizerFactory=\
com.thaap.payments.support.ExclusiveMeterRegistryContextCustomizerFactory
